// flags H / V / S; 736 block starts incl. the 256 cell table entries, 256 cells and 128 Duff entries) through run_animation_machine only.
// Inputs are declared fixtures: work RAM filled by a declared LCG (seed per row; 0 = zero RAM) with LONG STOP at 10f000..10f01c and the
// row's "address:bytes" items (applied in order), declared registers, the incoming C and the incoming PVC bank. Synthetic typed physical
// bytes (not a ROM oracle and not ROM data): first-level frame pointer tables in the bank windows (physical 200000 + n * 100000 + 4 +
// index) and one second-level table + frame inside the bank 0 window; sprite entries, second-level tables and frames otherwise in RAM.
// The FIXTURES/BLOCKS tables were produced from the original code bytes (Unicorn M68000, observer PvcMachine with the same synthetic
// bytes overlaid, write-protected fixed ROM, stack in work RAM, every banked data read checked to stay inside the synthetic bytes, no
// fixed-ROM data read, no device read; scratch generator outside the repository): each success row records the native stop state (16
// registers and the FNV-1a digest of RAM, D0-D7/A0-A7, PC, bank, reads, status and the ordered ports incl. every MOVE.L Dn,(A6) video
// event and the PVC bank writes). Rows stop at the final RTS to STOP, at a declared stop, or (block rows) at the next block start. The
// expected C is the contract classification (the 8 table slots and the 256 cell table entries are FLOW_ONLY; H4 has no carry consumer
// and no known-carry producer).
